# Lua conventions

## Modules

- Dot paths from repo root: `require "word_game.ui.letter_card_faces"`
- Package folders use `init.lua`
- Most modules: `local M = {}` … `return M`
- Pure data configs may `return { ... }` directly (`deck_face_colors.lua`)

## Naming

- Files/dirs: `snake_case`
- Locals: `snake_case`
- Classes/globals: `PascalCase` (`Card`, `Game`, `LayoutView`)
- Package globals: `UPPER_SNAKE` (`WORD_GAME`, `G`, `DEVTOOLS`)
- Feature flags on `G`: `F_*` from `runtime_options.flags`

## Classes (`app/core/object.lua`)

```lua
Card = EaseNode:derive("Card")

function Card:construct(X, Y, W, H, ...)
    EaseNode.construct(self, X, Y, W, H)
end
```

Chain: `Object → Node → EaseNode/Moveable → Sprite, LayoutView, Card, CardArea`

`card.lua` mixes in behavior via requires (`card_visuals.lua`, `card_ui.lua`) — preserve this pattern.

## Callbacks & layout

- UI binds `G.FUNCS.*` by string — move implementations, not registration names
- Model requests layout via `WORD_GAME.Layout.request_refresh()` / deferred `G.ARGS.pending_layout` — not direct geometry from model code

## Annotations

Add `---@class` / `---@field` on new public APIs. Analyzer stubs live in `types/`; `.emmyrc.json` ignores `_tools/`.

## Do not hand-edit

`dictionary/words_set.lua`, regenerated `deck_face_colors.lua`, binary textures — use `_tools/` scripts.
